{"availability":"available","full":"jd-opensource/JoyAI-Video-Edit","name":"JoyAI-Video-Edit","description":"[Official Repo] JoyAI-Video-Edit: Real-Time Open-Ended Video Editing with Autoregressive Diffusion","category":"Other","language":"Python","stars":1917,"forks":111,"created":"2026-08-04T08:22:24Z","updated":"2026-09-23T10:27:51Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":[],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/wxDai/joyai-video-edit","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.048Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.048Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.048Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.048Z","stars":1917,"forks":111}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["JoyAI-Video-Edit is a real-time, instruction-guided video editing system for open-ended video streams. Given a live camera stream or uploaded video and a natural-language edit instruction, it edits frames causally as they arrive, without waiting for the full video, requiring a predefined video length, or revisiting future frames. In our deployment benchmark, the full end-to-end pipeline reaches 30 FPS at 720 × 1248, pushing video editing from offline batch processing toward interactive streaming generation.","The system combines an MLLM-based condition encoder, a causal video VAE, and a 16B-parameter multimodal diffusion transformer. It is trained and deployed as an autoregressive diffusion editor, then accelerated with aligned autoregressive distribution matching distillation, long-horizon optimization, bounded KV-state inference, and deployment-oriented scheduling to sustain high-throughput 720p editing while reducing train-inference mismatch and accumulated temporal drift."],"features":["Real-time open-ended editing. Edits live or uploaded videos as frames arrive, without requiring the full sequence upfront.","Diverse instruction control. Supports subject edits, local edits, background changes, style transfer, motion changes, and reference-guided editing.","Autoregressive diffusion design. Combines an MLLM condition encoder, causal video VAE, and MMDiT backbone for streaming video editing.","High-throughput 720p deployment. Reaches 30 FPS end-to-end throughput at 720 × 1248 with bounded KV-state inference and stable per-chunk compute."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoyAI-Video-Edit/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"ebcaadb19d0577c9b18dc3b14aef9b93d2c4e8e80a366bfbc9311f660820ce45","extractedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.166Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.166Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"JoyAI-Video-Edit is a real-time, instruction-guided video editing system for open-ended video streams. Given a live camera stream or uploaded video and a natural-language edit instruction, it edits frames causally as they arrive, without waiting for the full video, requiring a predefined video length, or revisiting future frames. In our deployment benchmark, the full end-to-end pipeline reaches 30 FPS at 720 × 1248, pushing video editing from offline batch processing toward interactive streaming generation.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoyAI-Video-Edit/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"ebcaadb19d0577c9b18dc3b14aef9b93d2c4e8e80a366bfbc9311f660820ce45","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoyAI-Video-Edit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.166Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-09-23T10:27:51Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jd-opensource/JoyAI-Video-Edit/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-05T21:32:14.167Z","hash":"ebcaadb19d0577c9b18dc3b14aef9b93d2c4e8e80a366bfbc9311f660820ce45","originalBytes":10118,"storedBytes":10118,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["video","joyai-video-edit","editing","diffusion","real-time","autoregressive","edits","live","zhang","demo","deploy","deployment","deployment.md